Local binary package build
==========================

This branch contains packaging only. Driver source remains on main.
Run from the repository root with main fetched and the packaging branch checked out:

    builddir=$(mktemp -d)
    mkdir "$builddir/source"
    git archive main | tar -x -C "$builddir/source"
    cp -a debian "$builddir/source/"
    cd "$builddir/source"
    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

Build dependencies: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-dkms,
device-tree-compiler, cpp. Output is in the parent of source/.
The source dkms.conf version must match the upstream changelog version.

Installation and scope
======================

This package targets 64-bit Raspberry Pi OS with /boot/firmware/overlays.
It requires both Pi 4 (rpi-v8) and Pi 5 (rpi-2712) headers so the same
package has the appropriate platform headers. Raspberry Pi's APT repository
must be configured. On the target, install the downloaded package with:

    sudo apt install ./rk628-rpi-dkms_0.1.0-1_all.deb

Update the target system and reboot first when its running kernel has no
matching installed headers. DKMS compilation does not test HDMI/CSI hardware.
Uninstall any previous manual installation before switching to this package;
the source installer and dpkg must not manage the same DKMS source or rules.

The package delivers driver sources and dkms.conf under /usr/src,
two compiled overlays under /boot/firmware/overlays, and vendor udev rules
under /usr/lib/udev/rules.d. DKMS manages module registration and removal.
The source installer POST_INSTALL hook is omitted from the packaged dkms.conf
because dpkg manages the overlays directly. Package removal removes these
files; boot configuration changes made by the user remain the user's task.

The package does not modify config.txt, activate an overlay, reboot,
install media-initd, or provide PiKVM OS packaging. Source installation on
other systems remains available from main. No automated publishing is
included at this stage.
